From: Paul-Louis Charrière <plcharriere@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 14:38:31 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7996: keep the default RTS threshold after a
 hardware restart

A radio without a configured RTS threshold starts with a threshold of
0x92b.  After a hardware restart, mac80211 sets the RTS threshold of
every radio again, which is -1 (off) for such a radio, and the firmware
gets 0xffffffff: RTS by frame length stays off until the radio starts
again.

Send 0x92b for a threshold of -1 in mt7996_mcu_set_rts_thresh(), so a
radio keeps the threshold it started with.  Turning RTS off while a
radio runs now also gives 0x92b, as turning it off before the radio
starts already did.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Paul-Louis Charrière <plcharriere@gmail.com>
---
--- a/mt7996/main.c
+++ b/mt7996/main.c
@@ -17,8 +17,7 @@ static u32 mt7996_rts_threshold(struct m
 		if (phy->dev->radio_phy[i] == phy)
 			val = wiphy->radio_cfg[i].rts_threshold;
 
-	/* without a configured threshold, keep the default one */
-	return val == (u32)-1 ? 0x92b : val;
+	return val;
 }
 
 int mt7996_run(struct mt7996_phy *phy)
--- a/mt7996/mcu.c
+++ b/mt7996/mcu.c
@@ -5494,7 +5494,8 @@ int mt7996_mcu_set_rts_thresh(struct mt7
 		.band_idx = phy->mt76->band_idx,
 		.tag = cpu_to_le16(UNI_BAND_CONFIG_RTS_THRESHOLD),
 		.len = cpu_to_le16(sizeof(req) - 4),
-		.len_thresh = cpu_to_le32(val),
+		/* RTS off (-1) gets the default threshold */
+		.len_thresh = cpu_to_le32(val == (u32)-1 ? 0x92b : val),
 		.pkt_thresh = cpu_to_le32(0x2),
 	};
 
